reading: for A >= 1 the barrier falls steeply with A -- a stiffer chain
has a wider core and a smoother PN landscape. Below A ~ 1 it is NOT
monotone, and that is tied to the 'min' column: WHICH symmetric state
is the minimum flips with (p,A). The flip is physics of the PN
landscape, not a bug, and it is why the barrier must be taken as a
|gap| between the two rather than assuming one of them wins.
At the standing p=8, A=1 the barrier is 2.2% of E_core.
Cross-check: the 'min' column agrees with charge_fk.c's independently
relaxed E_core at every (p,A) they share.
Rows marked '< 1e-12' are below the FP floor: the half-shifted seed
relaxed back into the minimum, i.e. no barrier is resolvable.

